  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFRC - Preparing for an Effective Response (PER) in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRCI</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening CRCI&#x2019;s disaster response capabilities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Society plays its auxiliary role, in accordance with the RCRC Movement Fundamental Principles, by strengthening local preparedness capacities to ensure rapid and effective humanitarian assistance to prevent and alleviate human suffering.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through a series of self-assessment workshops, five key PER components were prioritized: logistics, epidemics preparedness, cash preparedness, auxiliary role and Disaster Risk Management policy. This process led to the development of a PER action plan with activities in these 5 focus areas.</narrative>
  </description>
